#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of GNOME Shell"
msgstr "Instalação do GNOME Shell"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:141
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>GNOME Shell</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""
"Instale o <application>GNOME Shell</application> executando os seguintes "
"comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:145
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release \\\n"
"            -Dsystemd=false     \\\n"
"            -Dtests=false       \\\n"
"            ..                  &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release \\\n"
"            -Dsystemd=false     \\\n"
"            -Dtests=false       \\\n"
"            ..                  &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:155
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release \\\n"
"            -Dtests=false       \\\n"
"            ..                  &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release \\\n"
"            -Dtests=false       \\\n"
"            ..                  &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"

#.  "Failed to read monitors config file
#.            '/home/xry111/.config/monitors.xml': Logical monitors not
#.            adjacent"
#.            The same thing happens in mutter but it's worked around with
#.            HOME="".  We cannot use HOME="" here or more tests will fail.
#.            We also cannot tell the users to remove monitors.xml because
#.            doing so will purge their monitor settings.  Maybe we can
#.            use bwrap to run the test with an empty tmpfs mounted on $HOME
#.            in a separate namespace, but it's too overkill IMO.
#.            DO NOT REMOVE unless you've tested with a "complex multi-monitor
#.            configuration" (with mixed scaling settings and "strange"
#.            positions of monitors).
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:165
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the results, you need to remove the "
"<parameter>-Dtests=false</parameter> switch, and to have <xref "
"linkend=\"mutter\"/> compiled and installed with tests also.  To run the "
"tests, issue: <command>ninja test</command>. You must be running an X "
"session to run the tests. Some will fail if <xref linkend=\"gdm\"/> is not "
"installed. <phrase revision=\"sysv\">Several more tests may fail in the Sysv"
" environment.</phrase> One test named <filename>CSS styling "
"support</filename> is known to fail with some multi-monitor configurations."
msgstr ""
"Para testar os resultados, você precisa remover a chave "
"<parameter>-Dtests=false</parameter> e ter o <xref linkend=\"mutter\"/> "
"compilado e instalado com testes também. Para executar os testes, emita: "
"<command>ninja test</command>. Você precisa estar executando uma sessão do X"
" para executar os testes. Alguns falharão se o <xref linkend=\"gdm\"/> não "
"estiver instalado. <phrase revision=\"sysv\">Vários outros testes "
"possivelmente falhem no ambiente Sysv.</phrase> Um teste chamado "
"<filename>CSS styling support</filename> é conhecido por falhar com algumas "
"configurações de vários monitores."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/gnome/platform/gnome-shell.xml:190
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

